  "name": "raytrace",
  "description": "A low-level hardware-accelerated raytracer prototype implemented in Rust using the legacy gfx-rs graphics stack. It utilizes GLFW for window management and OpenGL-based shaders to project and display raytraced buffers directly to the screen via texture manipulation. The implementation demonstrates early idiomatic Rust patterns such as procedural macros for shader parameters and vertex format declarations.",
